🪜 Climbing Stairs (DP)
🧠 Problem

Given n steps, you can climb:

1 step OR 2 steps at a time

👉 Find total distinct ways to reach step n

🔑 Core Idea (MOST IMPORTANT)

👉 Think backward, not forward

At step i, you ask:

“Where did I come from?”

from i-1 (1 step)
from i-2 (2 steps)
🔁 Recurrence

dp[i]=dp[i−1]+dp[i−2]

👉 Total ways = sum of ways from previous steps

🧱 State Definition
dp[i] = number of ways to reach step i
🧩 Base Cases
dp[0] = 1   // already at step 0 (1 way: do nothing)
dp[1] = 1   // only one way: take 1 step
⚙️ DP Construction (Bottom-Up)

👉 Build from smallest → largest

int climbStairs(int n) {
    int[] dp = new int[n + 1];

    dp[0] = 1;
    dp[1] = 1;

    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2];
    }

    return dp[n];
}
